Sophie: heads up — opened a docs PR for rate limits / quotas / usage analytics updates: https://github.com/redwood-inference/docs/pull/142. Main asks: clarify "metering" language, add an SDK snippet showing retry/backoff for 429s, and update the Console dashboard screenshots to include per-route token breakdowns. PTAL when you have a moment :pray:
Jordan: looking now. do you want the dashboard screenshot to show 'per-route' or 'per-model' first?
Sophie: per-route is higher priority for customers migrating from legacy metering. we should still show a small 'per-model' tile as optional in the dashboard gallery.
Maya: quick question about metering wording — your doc says "billing is per request or per-token depending on plan". can we be explicit about which plan uses which meter? customers will ask.
Sophie: yes good call. propose: "Free & Starter: per-request meter (counted as API calls). Standard & Enterprise: per-token meter (counts input+output tokens)." also call out a grace cap for Starter (first 100k tokens free) 
Ada: I'll add an SDK snippet demonstrating exponential backoff on 429s. Suggestion for snippet (JS):
```
async function sendWithRetry(req, retries = 5) {
  for (let i = 0; i < retries; i++) {
    try {
      return await client.generate(req);
    } catch (err) {
      if (err.status === 429 && i < retries - 1) {
        await new Promise(r => setTimeout(r, Math.pow(2, i) * 200 + Math.random() * 100));
        continue;
      }
      throw err;
    }
  }
}
```
Ada: will also include a short Python example with tenacity.
doc-lint-bot: found 2 link-name mismatches in the PR (docs/usage/quotas.md -> anchor changed). See inline suggestions.
Sophie: thanks bot — I'll fix the anchors. Matt can you sign off on the tier wording? want to avoid accidentally implying feature parity across Standard vs Enterprise.
Matt: saw the PR. Wording looks fine but please change "Standard & Enterprise: per-token" -> "Standard (metered primarily per-token) and Enterprise (per-token with optional committed tiers)" — we need the committed tiers callout. also add a one-line note that Enterprise customers can choose meter mode at onboarding.
Sophie: updated the text in the PR to include that phrasing. added a short FAQ entry "How do I choose a metering mode?"
Jordan: I'll replace screenshots — heads up, Console changed the dropdown from 'routes' to 'endpoints' last month, so take a screenshot from staging. also adding an example Saved Query for per-route token spend: `SELECT route, sum(tokens) as tokens FROM usage WHERE org_id = :org GROUP BY route ORDER BY tokens DESC LIMIT 10`
Maya: tiny wording nit — in the "Rate limit examples" section you have a table showing "100 rps" for Starter. could we add a real-world mapping line e.g., "~25 short chat requests/s (avg 512 tokens)" to help customers understand?
Sophie: great idea — I'll add that line under each tier.
Ben: Support can draft a migration blurb for existing Dedicated customers (how their quotas map to the new per-token meters). I can have a 3-bullet draft by EOD.
Sophie: perfect, please drop it as a comment on the PR so we can copy it into the migration guide.
Ada: pushed the JS + Python snippets to the PR and added test snippets for 429 retry behavior.
doc-lint-bot: all link-name mismatches resolved. one remaining suggestion: prefer ${{token_cost}} notation consistently in pricing examples.
Sophie: updated placeholders to ${{token_cost}}. can folks review the wording around "grace cap" and the FAQ? requesting reviews from @Jordan @Matt @Maya @Ada.
Jordan: approving once screenshots are uploaded.
Matt: approved (wording fix applied).
Maya: left one tiny grammar suggestion, otherwise LGTM.
Ben: posted the Dedicated -> per-token migration blurb in PR comments.
Sophie: thanks everyone — I'll merge after screenshots and then file a short changelog note for the docs release. :tada:
